-- Baseline: consolidated Phase 2-7 schema (previous 28 incremental migrations).
--
-- These migrations were squashed on 2026-10-03. Prisma Migrate has no
-- automatic rollback, so squashing is only safe while no database has been
-- deployed from the old history. That precondition holds: production
-- PostgreSQL is still an open provisioning item, so the superseded migrations
-- were never applied anywhere. The original files remain in the git history.
--
-- This baseline is generated by Prisma from prisma/schema.prisma
-- (migrate diff --from-empty --to-schema-datamodel), so it reproduces the
-- current schema exactly rather than replaying hand-written DDL. Verified by
-- comparing the statement set of this file plus
-- 20261003100000_add_enterprise_sso against a full --from-empty diff: all
-- 1061 statements match.
--
-- The previous migrations were pure DDL. They contained no CREATE EXTENSION,
-- function, trigger, row-level-security policy, partial index, materialized
-- view or data backfill, so nothing outside the datamodel is lost here.
--
-- Enterprise SSO is deliberately excluded from the baseline and applied by the
-- next migration, so it keeps its own release boundary.

-- CreateSchema
